msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:212
msgid "Use `Ctrl+Alt+R` to run tasks quickly"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:213
msgid "Lean on your terminal (`Alt+F12`) for anything tasks don't cover"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:215
msgid "No Framework Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:217
msgid ""
"WebStorm's value for web development comes largely from its framework "
"integration. React components get special treatment. Angular has dedicated "
"tooling. Vue single-file components are fully understood. The npm tool "
"window shows all your scripts."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:219
msgid ""
"Zed has none of this built-in. The TypeScript language server sees your code "
"as TypeScript—it doesn't understand that a function is a React component or "
"that a file is an Angular service."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:223
msgid ""
"Use grep and file search liberally. `Cmd+Shift+F` with a regex can find "
"component definitions, route configurations, or API endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:224
msgid ""
"Rely on your language server's \"find references\" (`Alt+F7`) for navigation—"
"it works, just without framework context"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:225
msgid ""
"Consider using framework-specific CLI tools (`ng`, `next`, `vite`) from "
"Zed's terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:226
msgid ""
"For React, JSX/TSX syntax and TypeScript types still provide good "
"intelligence"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:228
msgid ""
"**Tip:** For projects with complex configurations, keep your framework's "
"documentation handy. Zed's speed comes with less hand-holding for framework-"
"specific features."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:230
msgid "Tool Windows vs. Docks"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/webstorm.md:232
msgid ""
"WebStorm organizes auxiliary views into numbered tool windows (Project = 1, "
"npm = Alt+F11, Terminal = Alt+F12, etc.). Zed uses a similar concept called "
"\"docks\":"
msgstr ""

